1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,500
Then a sound you feel in your chest.
Far behind you. A horn.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,367
Rule thirteen! A horn means flatten!
Backs to the wall!

3
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:14,133
Four hundred backs hit the cold tiles.
A diesel rescue cart crawls past on
the next track. Inches away.

4
00:00:14,833 --> 00:00:19,233
Pressed to the wall, your lungs start
to whistle. You can't move. You can't
cough.

5
00:00:19,933 --> 00:00:24,300
Rescue crew. Diesel engine. They're
checking the line. That's good news.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
The cart stops. A worker swings a
lantern and waves the line forward.

7
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,500
My train! I dropped my train!

8
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:36,300
Eli's little toy train slips off the
ledge and lands between the rails.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,700
Rule fourteen. Never go back for
something you dropped. Never.

10
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,700
But my dad gave it to me.

11
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,233
I know, buddy. I'm sorry. Hold my
strap.
